### 1.  A construction with 16 stones  

Consider the residue  

\[
\phi(r,c)=r+2c\pmod 5 .
\]

Place a black stone on **every** square for which  

\[
\phi(r,c)=4 .
\]

On a \(9\times 9\) board there are exactly  

\[
\bigl\lvert\{(r,c):0\le r,c\le 8,\;r+2c\equiv4\pmod5\}\bigr\rvert =16
\]

such squares (the pattern is shown below).

```
..X....X.
....X....
.X....X..
...X....X
X....X...
..X....X.
....X....
.X....X..
...X....X
```

